From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:50:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: surface-laptop8: Clear
 GUSB3PIPECTL.DEPOCHANGE on the Type-C DWC3s

GUSB3PIPECTL.DEPOCHANGE reads as set on these controllers, and Linux
leaves it set unless told otherwise. With it set, the controller delays
the PHY power state change when the SuperSpeed link enters U1, U2 or U3.

When the SuperSpeed port of a Type-C controller is tunnelled through the
USB4 host router, that power state handshake is with the router's USB3
adapter instead of the combo PHY, and with DEPOCHANGE set the tunnelled
link does not leave U2 or U3. A hub behind a USB4 dock entered U2 and
never returned to U0, so control transfers to it timed out, and resuming
it from U3 ended in a disconnect and re-enumeration. With the bit
cleared, U2 exit and U3 resume across the tunnel work.

Set snps,dis-del-phy-power-chg-quirk, which clears the bit, on the
Surface Laptop 8's two Type-C controllers. The setting applies to the
port whether or not it is tunnelled; native USB3 links were seen working
with the bit set and with it cleared. The platform's Windows driver
clears the same bit on these controllers. Other Glymur boards, which do
not describe a USB4 host router, are left unchanged.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts
index ebdd491a7a3..4cc0be5deb9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts
@@ -970,6 +970,8 @@ embedded-controller {
 &usb_0 {
 	/* Dual role: UCSI over the SOCCP drives the role switch. */
 	dr_mode = "otg";
+	/* U2/U3 exit across a USB4 tunnel needs GUSB3PIPECTL.DEPOCHANGE clear. */
+	snps,dis-del-phy-power-chg-quirk;
 
 	status = "okay";
 };
@@ -1013,6 +1015,7 @@ &usb_0_qmpphy_out {
 
 &usb_1 {
 	dr_mode = "otg";
+	snps,dis-del-phy-power-chg-quirk;
 
 	status = "okay";
 };
